{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduleSession"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sessions can be either trading or non-trading, with different sets of rules and reasons to exist."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Sessions do not overlap with each other - rather they form consecutive chain of adjacent periods of time that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cover entire time scale. The point on a border line is considered to belong to following session that starts there."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Each session completely fits inside a certain day. Day may contain sessions with zero duration - e.g. indices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that post value once a day. Such sessions can be of any appropriate type, trading or non-trading."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:15DXFeedFramework15ScheduleSessionC","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleSession","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScheduleSession","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScheduleSession","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Class","modules":[{"name":"DXFeedFramework"}],"symbolKind":"class"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.dxfeed.DXFeedFramework\/documentation\/DXFeedFramework\/ScheduleSession"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Session represents a continuous period of time during which apply same rules regarding trading activity."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example, regular trading session is a period of time consisting of one day of business activities"},{"type":"text","text":" "